## 5. Insights

- `spr.naive`: 22% of the scalar add peak, 5% of the SIMD peak, 5% of the roofline (geomean). 0/16 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - Far below every ceiling: neither DRAM bandwidth nor the add units are the limit. The time goes into latency: index loads, gathers, short loops with data-dependent trip counts (branch mispredicts).
  - ns/add rises strongly with k in 16/16 cases: larger k saves additions but each one costs more.
- `spr.v0`: 23% of the scalar add peak, 6% of the SIMD peak, 6% of the roofline (geomean). 0/16 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - Far below every ceiling: neither DRAM bandwidth nor the add units are the limit. The time goes into latency: index loads, gathers, short loops with data-dependent trip counts (branch mispredicts).
  - ns/add rises strongly with k in 16/16 cases: larger k saves additions but each one costs more.
- `spr.v1`: 24% of the scalar add peak, 6% of the SIMD peak, 6% of the roofline (geomean). 0/16 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - Far below every ceiling: neither DRAM bandwidth nor the add units are the limit. The time goes into latency: index loads, gathers, short loops with data-dependent trip counts (branch mispredicts).
  - ns/add rises strongly with k in 16/16 cases: larger k saves additions but each one costs more.
- `spr.v2.b32`: 101% of the scalar add peak, 25% of the SIMD peak, 25% of the roofline (geomean). 0/16 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
- `spr.v3.b32.u1`: 100% of the scalar add peak, 25% of the SIMD peak, 25% of the roofline (geomean). 0/16 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - Far below every ceiling: neither DRAM bandwidth nor the add units are the limit. The time goes into latency: index loads, gathers, short loops with data-dependent trip counts (branch mispredicts).
- `spr.v4.b32`: 141% of the scalar add peak, 35% of the SIMD peak, 35% of the roofline (geomean). 0/16 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
  - ns/add rises strongly with k in 15/16 cases: larger k saves additions but each one costs more.
- `spr.v5.b32`: 141% of the scalar add peak, 35% of the SIMD peak, 35% of the roofline (geomean). 0/16 points sit left of the ridge (DRAM-bound roof).
